  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "r57-2175-enclosure",
      "topic": "2175 complete eight-question authorial enclosure and cover/enclosure dates",
      "requirement": "Preserve 2175 as a copy of Darwin’s cover and complete eight-question enclosure. Cover composition November 23 differs from November 22 enclosure signature. The Gwatkin passage quoted through Hamilton Smith is authorial enclosure content and may remain as an attributed quotation inside Darwin prose. It is neither an editorial footnote nor an incoming answer. Exclude editorial footnote markers/prose and later January 13 Buist routing note. Enclosure heading and closing dateline are structural metadata, not prose to insert into final content.",
      "source_layer_requirements": [
        "All eight numbered questions occur under div.enclosures/div.enclosure/p[1] through p[8]; ninth paragraph is signature and November22 dateline. Nested Gwatkin/Smith quotation in first question remains attributed and distinct from Darwin’s own request.",
        "Later routing note supplies provenance only, not a recovered answer or November delivery."
      ],
      "source_ids": [
        "DCP-LETT-2175"
      ],
      "exact_source_evidence": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "You told me that you thought you could obtain information for me about the colours and markings of some Indian horses, from the very best authority, namely Col. E. Dickie. If you could interest him to oblige me with answers to the following questions, it would be conferring a very great kindness on me.",
          "char_start": 0,
          "char_end": 303,
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[2]"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "body_paragraph": 3,
          "quote": "Would you be so kind as to send off my queries pretty soon, as time is precious.",
          "char_start": 0,
          "char_end": 80,
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[4]"
        }
      ],
      "source_provenance": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "source_path": "data/raw/dcp/1856-1857/pages/DCP-LETT-2175.html",
          "source_html_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530",
          "xml_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/expansions/1856-1857/letters/DCP-LETT-2175.xml",
          "xml_sha256": "48cb3ff16c9bdb7f397d1ab22f0ba7a704cf06e21b0b5126d1996c35773fd7f2",
          "verified_xml_dates": [
            {
              "text": "23 Nov 1857",
              "attributes": {
                "when": "1857-11-23"
              },
              "lower": "1857-11-23",
              "upper": "1857-11-23",
              "xml_fragment": "<ns0:date xmlns:ns0=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" when=\"1857-11-23\">23 Nov 1857</ns0:date>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "enclosure_proof": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "enclosure_paragraph": 1,
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/div/p[1]",
          "text_without_footnote_markers": "1. Major Gwatkin in a letter published by Col. Hamilton Smith, speaking of the Kutch or Kahleawar breed of horses, says “Kutch is the country where the mares are bred; the sire is an Arab. They are generally greys or light duns, and almost invariably have the zebra-marks on the arms and thighs with list down the back.” I am very anxious to know what are the colours of the pure Kutch mares; for it seems very surprising that the offspring, begotten by Arab sires, which I believe are never dun, should be generally dun or grey and have a dorsal stripe and transverse zebra-like marks on the legs. These latter characteristics, I hear, are generally lost in the Scandinavian duns, when crossed with any other colour.",
          "role": "authorial_question",
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "enclosure_paragraph": 2,
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/div/p[2]",
          "text_without_footnote_markers": "2. In the Kutch or Kahleawar duns (whether or not a crossed breed), are the zebra-like leg-markings, and dorsal stripe very generally present? Does a transverse shoulder stripe, like that on the ass, ever occur? Is such shoulder stripe ever double, as sometimes, though very rarely, is the case with the ass.",
          "role": "authorial_question",
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "enclosure_paragraph": 3,
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/div/p[3]",
          "text_without_footnote_markers": "3. Am I to understand from Major Gwatkin that the Grey Kutch horses have a dorsal stripe and zebra-like marks on the legs: I have never heard of this before.",
          "role": "authorial_question",
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "enclosure_paragraph": 4,
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/div/p[4]",
          "text_without_footnote_markers": "4. Are any Kutch horses cream-coloured; and have such the dorsal, or shoulder, or leg stripes?",
          "role": "authorial_question",
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "enclosure_paragraph": 5,
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/div/p[5]",
          "text_without_footnote_markers": "5. Chesnut horses often have a dorsal stripe: in India have they ever a shoulder or leg stripes?",
          "role": "authorial_question",
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "enclosure_paragraph": 6,
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/div/p[6]",
          "text_without_footnote_markers": "6. Is the dun or other colour when accompanied by the above stripes, strongly inherited, when such coloured horses are crossed with others.",
          "role": "authorial_question",
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "enclosure_paragraph": 7,
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/div/p[7]",
          "text_without_footnote_markers": "7. Are all the horses, whatever their colour may be, when striped, small and built like cobs.",
          "role": "authorial_question",
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "enclosure_paragraph": 8,
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/div/p[8]",
          "text_without_footnote_markers": "8. What is the colour of the Dun or Cream or other colour, when accompanied by stripes in the foal, before first hair is shed? Are the stripes at this early age more or less conspicuous?",
          "role": "authorial_question",
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2175",
          "enclosure_paragraph": 9,
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/div/p[9]",
          "text_without_footnote_markers": "C. Darwin Down, | Nov. 22nd 1857.",
          "role": "signature_and_dateline",
          "source_sha256": "90d7c504c3f2cfeeb00e11a28f56b9fe0bbf1fc62d7d2434500479e94c65c530"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "r57-mantell-mixed",
      "topic": "Mantell mixed hands and answer chronology",
      "requirement": "Keep DCP-LETT-6520 as a mixed document: Darwin questions occupy P1 and P3, while Mantell answers occupy P2 and P4-P6. Do not export it as a single-voice letter or use its broad before-10-April assignment to date every answer. DCP-LETT-1663 P5 is a contemporaneous Darwin fear that Mantell may not answer the beauty question, and DCP-LETT-1892 has four discrete possible years (1856, 1857, 1858, 1859); neither authorizes turning the later “Yes” into a precisely dated reply.",
      "source_layer_requirements": [
        "6520 retained body uses source path data/raw/dcp/1844-1846/pages/DCP-LETT-6520.html and accepted prior-reading provenance; pin its mixed-author paragraph boundaries and do not infer receipt from page order.",
        "The 1663 text contains a preserved artifact “obliged to for”; hold for evidence-based repair unless authoritative markup supports a correction."
      ],
      "source_ids": [
        "DCP-LETT-1663",
        "DCP-LETT-1892",
        "DCP-LETT-6520"
      ],
      "exact_source_evidence": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1663",
          "body_paragraph": 5,
          "quote": "Lastly, I fear you cannot answer my question whether the beau ideal of beauty amongst the less civilised natives (ie those least influenced by being accustomed to European faces) would agree with ours; viz whether we & they would pick out the same kind of beauty.— Forgive me if you can, & believe me,",
          "char_start": 0,
          "char_end": 301,
          "source_sha256": "445e13eae4d3c6b1a1a85a1b094e3ebce5f098099e8c3260405caeb126b41a7a",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div/div[1]/div[2]/p[6]"
